This is episode five of Not Built For This, The Little Levy That Could. The year I moved to California, it barely rained at all. It was 2015, and the local news was doing lots of stories about taking shorter showers and how much water it takes to grow a single almond. For most of my time in the state, California has been hovering somewhere between extreme and exceptional drought conditions. But then came the winter of 2023. The rain started on New Year's Eve. At first it was relieving, exciting even, to see the dry creek beds spring to life, and the sun-baked hills behind my house

