Jose scrolls through a chart that lists the strongest flows from the past. It goes back decades. Today is when Jose was a young man, and the river was running so high that it threatened to break through the old levee and flood the town. And it seems like he was here for pretty much all of those high water days, down by the river, fighting to prevent a flood. I was in that flood fight, and I was in that flood fight. Wow. And I remember that one too.

