I mean, you're using nature and in this sense, the floodplain, the floodplain is what we're using. It's a storage facility, plain and simple. They drew up a plan for this new setback levee. And as part of the proposal, the Nature Conservancy agreed to buy the 1,400 acres of farmland between the river and the new levy and donate it to the project. That land value would count as Hamilton City's local contribution to the cost of the project.

