plus the dollar value of the flood risk reduction, that's where we get the total benefits. And this time, the benefits were greater than the costs. Hamilton City passed the test, and the Corps gave the project their seal of approval. The new levy was deemed worth it, all because of the habitat restoration. And you might be thinking, great, problem solved.

